{
  "markdown": "# Engagement ad objective  | LinkedIn Help\n\nIncrease engagement on your content through likes, comments, shares, follows, and clicks to a landing page or LinkedIn Page when you select engagement as your ad set objective. The engagement ad objective is in the middle of the marketing funnel, which aims to help your audiences consider your business for their needs. \n\n## Available ad formats, bidding strategies, and optimization goals\n\nWe surface only ad formats, bidding strategies, and optimization goals that support your objective of increasing engagement. Engagement clicks are selected as your optimization goal by default. \n\nThe ad formats, bidding strategies, and optimization goals available vary depending on the setting. Learn more about the available options in the following table:\n\n| Setting | Available options\n\n| Ad formats | \n\n- \nSingle image\n\n- \nCarousel image\n\n- \nVideo\n\n- \nEvent\n\n- \nDocument\n\n- Thought leader\n\n- Article and newsletter\n\n- \nConversation\n\n- \nFollower\n\n| Bidding strategies | \n\n- \nMaximum delivery (automated)\n\n- \nCost cap\n\n- \nManual bidding\n\n| Optimization goals | \n\n- \nEngagement clicks\n\n- \nImpressions\n\n- \nSends (Sponsored Messaging ad formats only)\n\n## Reporting metrics\n\nGetting people to engage with your content is the key result of engagement ad sets. View a wide variety of reporting metrics from the Campaign Manager reporting dashboard, including: \n\n- Performance metrics \n\n- Engagement \n\n- Conversions \n\n- Bid and Budget \n\nYou can also view professional demographic data about members who are interacting with your ads. \n\nLearn more\n\n- [Chargeable clicks for engagement ad sets](https://www.linkedin.com/help/lms/answer/a424254)\n\n- [Objective-based reporting with key results](https://www.linkedin.com/help/lms/answer/a422642)\n\n- [Thought leader ads](https://www.linkedin.com/help/lms/answer/a1399568)\n\n- [Article and newsletter ads](https://www.linkedin.com/help/lms/answer/a5966218)\n\n- [Flexible ads](https://www.linkedin.com/help/lms/answer/a8635043)",
